    "resume":  {
                   "text":  "Rejo Z Mathew\nLocation: Chicago, IL\n\nSummary\nSenior data, analytics, and AI leader with 18+ years of experience modernizing enterprise data ecosystems, building scalable cloud-native data platforms, and driving AI/ML-powered transformation across financial services. Expert in governance, compliance, and customer-centric analytics. Proven leader of global teams and partner to C-suite stakeholders.\n\nCore Competencies\n- Enterprise data and AI strategy, architecture, and modernization\n- Cloud-native data platforms and analytics ecosystems (AWS, Snowflake, Spark)\n- AI/ML enablement and operationalization (MLOps, feature stores, model governance)\n- Knowledge graph and semantic layer design (Neo4j, AtScale)\n- Predictive analytics and decision intelligence (segmentation, propensity, optimization)\n- Data governance, quality, controls, and regulatory compliance\n- Customer-centric analytics and personalization\n- Metadata, lineage, observability, and platform reliability\n- Cross-functional leadership (technology, risk, product, marketing, business)\n- Global team development, data literacy, and change leadership\n\nProfessional Experience\nCapital One Financial (formerly Discover Financial Services), Chicago\nSr. Director, Data Science \u0026 Data Infrastructure Management, DNA (Jun 2022 - Present)\n- Led enterprise data and AI platform transformation with AWS/Snowflake for scalability and ML readiness\n- Built enterprise identity knowledge graph (Neo4j) and Customer 360 platform\n- Integrated MarTech, CRM, digital, and core banking data enabling AI-driven personalization ($100M gains)\n- Led data workstreams for student-loan portfolio migration and divestiture\n- Partnered with C-level executives on enterprise data and AI strategy and adoption\n- Led global organization of ~75 across data science, analytics, and engineering\n\nDirector, Data Science, Consumer Banking (Oct 2018 - Jun 2022)\n- Built and scaled ML feature store for enterprise AI/ML use cases\n- Delivered self-service BI for consumer banking business lines\n- Designed regulatory remediation and reporting frameworks; centralized control management\n- Served as Chief Data Steward for Consumer Banking\n\nSr. Manager, Analytics, BI \u0026 Pricing (Jul 2016 - Oct 2018)\n- Built analytical data environment and BI infrastructure post-origination migration\n- Developed multi-touch attribution model for marketing investment decisions\n- Redesigned risk-based pricing models; improved ROE and conversion\n\nManager, Analytics \u0026 Data Management (Jul 2014 - Jul 2016)\n- Managed operational analytics and business management reporting for Discover Home Loans\n\nProject Manager, Analytics (Apr 2012 - Jul 2014)\n- Delivered business analytics and management reporting for Discover Home Loans\n\nPrevious Experience\nSenior Business Analyst, American Express (Apr 2010 - Apr 2012)\nSenior Consultant (Summer Associate), Deloitte Consulting LLP (Jun 2008 - Aug 2008)\nAssistant System Engineer, Tata Consultancy Services (Feb 2007 - Jul 2007)\nSenior Software Engineer, UST Global (Dec 2003 - Oct 2006)\n\nEducation\n- Chief Digital Officer Program, Kellogg School of Management (2024)\n- MBA, Indiana University (2009)\n- B.Tech., University of Kerala (2003)\n\nCertifications\n- Certified Data Management Professional (CDMP)\n- AWS Certified Cloud Practitioner\n- Machine Learning Engineering for Production (MLOps)\n\nPortfolio\n- Enterprise Identity Graph\n- Self-Service BI and Analytics Enablement",
